CHANGELOG = '## [0.280.0] - a bank\'s rooms lit and floored as the walker\'s bank comps\n\nThe walker, 2026-10-27: "we need to prioritize a great looking bank interior next", with twelve comps (the factory\'s\ndocs/reference/BANK_INTERIOR_COMPS.md). The comps show "bright, even ceilings" in every public room, terrazzo or pale\ntile under the public in five of twelve, and the money "in hard rooms ... all lit by bare tubes".\n\nMeasured before on bank_branch_a02 (the factory\'s docs/findings/bank_interior/):\n\n- the lobby carpeted maroon under one lamp a 39 m2, a mean of 37 under the level\'s light;\n- the vault floor under bare bulbs, one a 55 m2, 30-40.\n\n### Added\n- **`lights.is_bank(business)`**, a whole word of the building\'s id, and **`bank_public(r, business)`**, its\n  `public_entry` rooms.\n- **A bank\'s public room is lit as a selling room** (`_selling_rooms`; `room_caps(..., selling=True)`): one lamp a\n  `_SELLING_M2_PER_LAMP` (25 m2), and the bake-only reach (`_bake_reach_rooms`, 0.279.0\'s).\n  - bank_branch_a02\'s lobby goes from 10 lamps to 15.\n  - bank_tower_a01\'s banking hall goes from 10 to 18. Its 4.2 m ceiling\'s row spacing holds it to one lamp a 40 m2.\n- **A bank\'s rooms below grade and over the take are lit by tubes** (`_tube_rooms`): ceiling rows of fluorescents\n  where every other building hangs moody bulbs. No bank in the library hangs a pendant now. bank_branch_a02\'s vault\n  goes from one lamp a 32 m2 to one a 16 m2.\n- **A bank\'s public floor is `tile`** (`floors.BANK_PUBLIC_FLOOR`). `floors._material` takes the building\'s\n  `business`, and `slab_slots` and `hole_causes._surface` both pass it, so the slab and the hole rule give one answer.\n  What the tile is, the theme\'s. Every other lobby keeps its carpet.\n\n### Fixed\n- **A row split into one-lamp runs carries the row\'s `bake_reach`.** The stamp read each run\'s own spacing, which is 0\n  for a run of one lamp. So the lamps over a split went without the bake-only reach. In a bank that is the line over\n  the teller counter; in a supermarket, the pieces of a split row.\n\n### Tests\n- `tests/test_bank_light_floor.py` (all fail on 0.279.0):\n  - a bank is a whole word;\n  - a bank\'s public floor is tile, another lobby keeps its carpet, a room\'s own material wins;\n  - the hole rule asks as the slab does;\n  - a bank\'s lobby is lit as a selling room and its money by tubes, while a cellar elsewhere stays moody (the\n    control);\n  - every built bank\'s public floor is tile, no room hangs a pendant, and every public row carries the reach.\n\n'
OLD_VERSION, NEW_VERSION = 'Deli Counter 0.279.0', 'Deli Counter 0.280.0'


def _sha(b):
    return hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest()[:16]


def _read(name):
    """The file's LF text and whether it is CRLF on disk; refuses mixed endings and a file that is not the pinned one."""
    raw = (REPO / name).read_bytes()
    crlf, lf = raw.count(b"\r\n"), raw.count(b"\n")
    if crlf not in (0, lf):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s has mixed line endings (%d CRLF of %d); nothing written"
                         % (name, crlf, lf))
    text = raw.decode("utf-8").replace("\r\n", "\n")
    if _sha(text.encode("utf-8")) != PINS[name]:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s is %s, not the %s this patch was written against; nothing "
                         "written" % (name, _sha(text.encode("utf-8")), PINS[name]))
    return text, crlf > 0


def main(argv):
    # every file worked out and checked before any is written
    out = {}
    for name, edits in EDITS.items():
        text, crlf = _read(name)
        for what, old, new in edits:
            if text.count(old) != 1:
                raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s: the anchor at %s is there %d times; nothing written"
                                 % (name, what, text.count(old)))
            text = text.replace(old, new)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    # a refurnished spec is carried whole, the file it replaces pinned like any other
    for name, text in REPLACED.items():
        _old, crlf = _read(name)
        out[name] = text.replace("\n", "\r\n") if crlf else text
    for name in NEW_FILES:
        if (REPO / name).exists():
            raise SystemExit("REFUSED: deli_counter/%s exists already; nothing written" % name)
    v = REPO / "VERSION"
    if v.read_bytes().decode("utf-8") != OLD_VERSION:
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: VERSION reads %r, not %s; nothing written" % (v.read_text(), OLD_VERSION))
    cl = REPO / "CHANGELOG.md"
    craw = cl.read_bytes()
    if b"\r\n" in craw or not craw.startswith(b"## [" + OLD_VERSION.split()[-1].encode() + b"]"):
        raise SystemExit("REFUSED: CHANGELOG.md is not LF opening on %s; nothing written" % OLD_VERSION)
    for name, text in out.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    for name, text in NEW_FILES.items():
        (REPO / name).write_bytes(text.encode("utf-8"))
    v.write_bytes(NEW_VERSION.encode("utf-8"))
    cl.write_bytes(CHANGELOG.encode("utf-8") + craw)
    print("%s applied: %d files edited, %d written, VERSION, CHANGELOG. Now, in deli_counter/: build.py --all, "
          "suite" % (NEW_VERSION, len(out), len(NEW_FILES)))
    return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
